    "result_text": "The acceptance test passes and the front-end typecheck is clean.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a home **Dashboard** showing client/project counts and the total money still owed, as a small additive full-stack change.\n\n**Server (OfficeFloor + Spring):**\n- `InvoiceRepository.sumOutstanding()` \u2014 a JPQL `SUM` over `UNPAID` invoices, `COALESCE`d to 0.\n- `DashboardSummary.java` \u2014 a read-only DTO carrying `clients`, `projects`, `outstanding`.\n- `DashboardSummaryGet.java` \u2014 logic class that reads the two repo `count()`s plus the outstanding sum in one request.\n- `rest/api/dashboard/summary.GET.yml` \u2014 wires `GET /api/dashboard/summary` (under `/api/` so it bypasses the SPA fallback).\n\n**Front-end (new files only):**\n- `features/dashboard/queries.ts` \u2014 `['dashboard']` query key + fetcher.\n- `features/dashboard/nav.slot.tsx` \u2014 fills `AppNav` with the `nav-dashboard` link.\n- `features/dashboard/DashboardSummary.tsx` \u2014 queries for itself; renders `dashboard-clients-count`, `dashboard-projects-count`, and `dashboard-outstanding-total` (2-decimal money formatting, matching the rest of the app).\n- `routes/dashboard.tsx` \u2014 the `/dashboard` page composing the summary.\n\n**No migration needed:** the change is a pure read-only aggregate over the existing `clients`/`projects`/`invoices` tables (with the existing `status` column), so there was no schema change to make \u2014 per CLAUDE.md, the change is only \"whatever the request needs.\" The existing `/__test__` seed already covers the fixture, so it was untouched, and the test asserts no audit records.\n\nThe test anchors matched exactly: counts `2`/`2` and outstanding `300.00` (the two UNPAID invoices, 100 + 200; the PAID 50 excluded).",
